  "goodToKnow": "Der Gesetzentwurf is a bill or draft law. In Germany, bills can be introduced by the federal government, members of the Bundestag or the Bundesrat. After three readings (Lesungen) in the Bundestag, the Bundesrat (representing the Länder) is involved, and finally the Federal President signs the law. Der Entwurf means draft or design. Also spelled Gesetzesentwurf. Plural: die Gesetzentwürfe."
